  "result": "**What it does:** Order utilities for a shop backend — `calcTotal` sums item price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies coupon codes, `averageItemPrice` averages, `formatOrder` renders an order to text.\n\n**Bugs:**\n1. `calcTotal` (line 5): `i <= items.length` overruns the array — reads `items[items.length]` (undefined) and throws on `.price`. Should be `i < items.length`.\n2. `averageItemPrice` (line 20): divides by zero for an empty array, returning `NaN`. Guard `items.length === 0`.\n3. `applyDiscount` (line 13): code lookup is case-sensitive and unvalidated — `discounts[code]` with a value like `\"constructor\"` hits prototype junk. Minor, but worth an `Object.hasOwn` check.",
